Elder Guardian: You've returned... but you've changed. I can see the emptiness where your light once shone. The Veil Maiden took something precious from you.
-> I lost them... Yin and Yang are gone
    <<jump acknowledge_loss>>
-> I feel hollow inside
    <<jump understand_pain>>
-> How do I move forward?
    <<jump path_forward>>
-> I need to be alone
    <<stop>>
===
title: acknowledge_loss
---
Elder Guardian: Yes... I felt their absence the moment you arrived. Those gentle spirits were part of you. Their loss is real, and your grief is valid.
-> Will they ever come back?
    <<jump truth_about_loss>>
-> I should have been stronger
    <<jump not_your_fault>>
-> What do I do now?
    <<jump path_forward>>
===
title: understand_pain
---
Elder Guardian: The Hollow Depths leave their mark on all who pass through. That emptiness you feel... it's the absence of connection, of light, of purpose.
-> How do I fill this void?
    <<jump path_forward>>
-> I've lost everything
    <<jump not_everything>>
-> Tell me about the Hollow Depths
    <<jump depths_explanation>>
===
title: truth_about_loss
---
Elder Guardian: I cannot lie to you. The Yin and Yang you knew... they cannot return as they were. The Veil Maiden's power consumed them utterly.
-> Then there's no hope?
    <<jump there_is_hope>>
-> I understand
    <<jump acceptance_path>>
===
title: not_your_fault
---
Elder Guardian: No, young one. You fought with all your strength. The Veil Maiden's battle was designed for you to lose. She isolates, she manipulates, she takes.
-> She planned this all along?
    <<jump veil_maiden_nature>>
-> I still feel responsible
    <<jump shared_burden>>
-> How do I stop her?
    <<jump path_forward>>
===
title: not_everything
---
Elder Guardian: You haven't lost everything. You're still here. You're still standing. And look around... others have walked this path. You're not alone.
-> Others have been hollowed too?
    <<jump the_lanterns>>
-> It doesn't feel like enough
    <<jump one_step>>
-> What should I do?
    <<jump path_forward>>
===
title: path_forward
---
Elder Guardian: The path forward is not one of vengeance, but of healing. Seek out The Lanterns - those who understand your pain. Together, you'll find strength.
-> Who are The Lanterns?
    <<jump the_lanterns>>
-> I want revenge on the Veil Maiden
    <<jump revenge_warning>>
-> I'll try to heal
    <<jump encouragement>>
===
title: there_is_hope
---
Elder Guardian: There is always hope, but it comes in forms we don't expect. Yin and Yang may be gone, but their essence... that can endure in different ways.
-> What do you mean?
    <<jump essence_endures>>
-> I'll find a way forward
    <<jump path_forward>>
===
title: acceptance_path
---
Elder Guardian: Understanding is the first step. Acceptance will come with time. For now, focus on rebuilding - yourself, and your connections to others.
-> How do I rebuild?
    <<jump path_forward>>
-> Thank you, Elder
    <<stop>>
===
title: veil_maiden_nature
---
Elder Guardian: The Veil Maiden isolates her victims, cuts them off from support, makes them dependent... then takes everything. She's done this before.
-> Then I'll make her pay
    <<jump revenge_warning>>
-> Has she done this to others?
    <<jump the_lanterns>>
-> How do I become stronger?
    <<jump path_forward>>
===
title: shared_burden
---
Elder Guardian: Responsibility is not yours alone to bear. We all saw the signs, the hub emptying, the light fading. We should have intervened sooner.
-> It's not your fault either
    <<jump mutual_understanding>>
-> What matters now is moving forward
    <<jump path_forward>>
===
title: the_lanterns
---
Elder Guardian: The Lanterns are ninjas who've also faced the Hollow Depths. They understand isolation, loss, and the slow climb back to the light. Seek them out.
-> Where can I find them?
    <<jump find_lanterns>>
-> Can they help me fight?
    <<jump lanterns_purpose>>
-> I'll look for them
    <<stop>>
===
title: one_step
---
Elder Guardian: Recovery doesn't happen all at once. One step, one conversation, one small victory. That's how the light returns.
-> I'll try
    <<jump encouragement>>
-> Where do I start?
    <<jump path_forward>>
===
title: revenge_warning
---
Elder Guardian: Vengeance born from pain leads only to more darkness. If you face her again, do so from a place of strength and healing, not hollow rage.
-> You're right. I need to heal first
    <<jump path_forward>>
-> I'll remember that
    <<stop>>
===
title: encouragement
---
Elder Guardian: That's all I ask. Take your time, reach out when you're ready, and remember - the hub may be dimmer, but it's not empty. We're still here.
<<fire_event act2_elder_conversation_complete>>
<<stop>>
